  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "pm_c",
      "defType": "meta/comment",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": -334
      },
      "params": {
        "text": "Preset Morph\n\nA spirograph instrument to perform with. Open the Presets panel: click a preset (Nebula, Clockwork, Urchin, Lace, Ember, Tide) to jump to it, or pick two under Morph and drag the slider between them — every slider glides at once and the drawing melts from one into the other. Vary (Ctrl/⌘+Shift+R) re-rolls the seed, which shifts each layer's phase. Drag the XY pad for zoom (left–right) and wobble (up–down), or drag on the preview to fan the layers apart and swell them, and tweak any slider, then save your own preset.\n\nHow it works: each layer is a hypotrochoid — a pen on a wheel of radius r rolling inside a ring of radius R — traced by a Curve node for Laps turns of the wheel in 1400 steps, wobbled along its length and drawn by a ForEach as a polygon; each layer's ring is 11 % smaller and turns a little faster. Presets store the sliders' values (and the seed) in the file; morphing interpolates them.",
        "width": 470,
        "height": 270
      }
    },
